## The rayshadow_glass.rib scene at 64 by 48: a matte sphere under a clear pane of two faces, lit by
## one distant light from above, so every shadow ray from the sphere crosses both faces at normal
## incidence. Kd 0.01 keeps interreflection, which only the path tracer renders, below the
## tolerance the test measures; the light makes up the radiance. Not third-party.
Display "glassparams_shadow.tif" "file" "rgba"
Format 64 48 1
PixelSamples 2 2
Option "pathtracer" "integer samples" [64]
Projection "perspective" "fov" [40]
Clipping 0.5 50
Translate 0 0 5
Rotate -20 1 0 0
WorldBegin
LightSource "distantlight" 1 "from" [0 10 0] "to" [0 0 0] "intensity" [230]
Surface "matte" "Kd" [0.01]
Sphere 1 -1 1 360
## begin pane
AttributeBegin
Surface "glass"
Polygon "P" [-2 2 -2  2 2 -2  2 2 2  -2 2 2]
Polygon "P" [-2 2.1 2  2 2.1 2  2 2.1 -2  -2 2.1 -2]
AttributeEnd
## end pane
WorldEnd
